Taken literally: Reading ?oG while confused is a bad idea. Also in
connection with mind flayers: They're called "mind flayers", not
"mindflayers". When you uncursed-geno "master mindflayers", the game tries
to parse that and gets stuck after "master", so it looks for the closest
match for "master", which happens to be a rank title of the monk class. If
you're playing a monk, you've just genocided yourself. I'm not aware of any
similar common mistakes with rank titles.

Concerning blessed genocide, which works by the letter representing a
monster on the screen, humans and elves are '@', dwarves are 'h', gnomes
are 'G', but the latter two shouldn't geno '@' anyway.


